==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|synæresis||dated}}
* {{alter|en|synairesis||uncommon}}
* {{alter|en|syneresis||US}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|συναίρεσις||unification}}, from {{m|grc|συν-||together}} + {{m|grc|αἵρεσις||taking}}, from {{m|grc|αἱρέω||I take}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sɪnˈɛrəsɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|synaereses}}
{{examples-right|sense=linguistics, prosody|examples=contraction of the ''-ew'' ({{IPAchar|/uː/|lang=en}}) and ''or-'' ({{IPAchar|/oʊɹ/|lang=en}}) of ''[[w:New Orleans|New Orleans]]'' into {{IPAchar|/ˈˈˈnɔːˈˈˈlənz/|lang=en}}.}}
# {{lb|en|linguistics|prosody}} the [[contraction]] of two [[vowel]]s into a [[diphthong]] or a [[long vowel]].
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} the [[separating]] out of the [[liquid]] from a [[gel]].

====Hypernyms====
* {{sense|linguistics|prosody}} {{l|en|metaplasm}}

====References====
* [http://rhetoric.byu.edu/figures/S/synaeresis.htm ''Silva Rhetoricae'' (rhetoric.byu.edu)]

